  "summary": "Missouri Gov. Mike Kehoe issued an executive order imposing new restrictions on ALPR use by state and local agencies receiving state funding, including a 30-day data deletion requirement, agency data ownership, prohibitions on non-law-enforcement use and AI facial recognition integration, and auditing requirements. Flock Safety said it supports strong guardrails.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "such users must permanently delete license plate and vehicle images within 30 days unless part of an \u201cactive and ongoing criminal investigation,\u201d or ongoing emergencies and missing person alerts.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "data captured by automated license plate reader systems is owned by the agency that uses the technology \u2014 not, for instance, vendors and contractors.",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "Agencies cannot integrate automatic AI-powered facial recognition into these tools",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    }
